# Only genuinely large, non-runtime files go through LFS.
#
# *.geojson used to be routed here too, which put two ~300KB files — one of them
# a runtime asset the map fetches — behind an authenticated LFS endpoint. When
# LFS auth fails on a server, git checks out a 130-byte pointer instead of the
# data, collectstatic happily publishes the pointer, and the alcaldías layer
# breaks with no error anywhere. Not worth it for 600KB.
designs/Assets.sketch filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.sketch filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
